patch type="fixed" "Data published right after `connect()` could be discarded without reporting an error in single peer connection and publisher-primary modes: the send path skipped the data channel open wait outside subscriber-primary, and a write handed to a channel that is still opening is evicted by the next one on the lossy channel's drop-oldest queue. Every send now waits for the specific channel (reliable or lossy) it will be written to, a send issued while the room is disconnected fails immediately instead of waiting out that timeout, and the first discarded write on a channel is now logged"
